>> title: Dosa
>> category: Flatbreads & Pancakes
>> tags: rice, lentils, fermented, indian, griddle
>> servings: 12
>> time: 20 hr
>> step.3: grind each smooth, combine with salt
>> step.4: ferment 10 hr until risen and bubbly
>> step.5: spread thin on a hot tawa, drizzle ghee, 2 min

Soak @idli rice{1 1/2%cup}(300 g; parboiled short-grain rice), @poha{2%Tbsp}(15 g; flattened rice), and @water{4%cup}(950 mL) for ~{5%hr}.

Soak @urad dal{1/2%cup}(100 g; skinned black gram), @fenugreek seeds{1/2%tsp}(2 g), and @water for the dal{2%cup}(475 mL) for ~{5%hr}.

Drain and grind @&(~2)soaked rice{} and @&(~1)soaked dal{} separately, then fold together with @fine sea salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g).

Ferment @&(~1)batter{} covered in a warm place ~{10%hr}, until risen and bubbly.

Spread @&(~1)batter{} thin on a hot #tawa{} and drizzle with @ghee{2%Tbsp}(28 g), ~{2%min}.
